window.QUESTIONS=[{"id":"FD1","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"Pace & delivery","weight":"critical","q":"Do we ship at the measured pace, go full time, or bring in a contractor?","lede":"One author touched every commit in 90 days; 24 weeks of appetite is 99 to 129 calendar weeks at the measured rate.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Measured pace","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Both founders full time"},{"title":"A contractor from day one"}],"rows":[{"label":"Calendar length for 24 weeks of appetite","cells":["99 to 129 weeks, at 1.21 commits a week","24 weeks, as written","About 8 weeks less than measured"]},{"label":"Which phases run now","cells":["0, A, B, D, H; E, F, G move to Later","Every phase as written","A and B run alongside D"]},{"label":"Who ships D and F","cells":["A contractor, if pace has not doubled","Sagnik and Amit","A contractor, from the start"]}],"note":"One author touched every commit in the last 90 days.","caption":"Three ways to spend the same 24 weeks of appetite."},"stakes":"Every date in the plan, and whether E, F and G survive as Later, depends on this one answer.","state":["10 distinct commit days in the last 58 days, 1.21 a week.","Since 1 September, 3 commits touched code and 111 touched documents.","One author on every commit in the last 90 days."],"tension":["The plan's 24-week appetite assumes a pace nobody has measured against it yet.","A contractor moves the pilot forward by about eight weeks, at a cost the plan has not priced."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship at the measured pace, publish dates every Friday","gains":["Dates match what is actually happening."],"costs":["Phases E, F and G move to Later."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Both founders go full time","gains":["The phase table stands as written."],"costs":["Needs income to cover both, unpriced here."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"None named in this plan."},{"k":"c","label":"Engage a contractor for phases D and F","gains":["Phases A and B run alongside D.","The pilot comes forward about eight weeks."],"costs":["A contractor's cost is not yet quoted."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"A contractor's fee, not yet quoted."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The measured pace is the only one with evidence behind it.","Dates published every Friday keep the promise honest either way."],"flip":"Two full months of commits at double today's rate would justify the full-time table without a contractor.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 1","git log on this repository, read 17 September 2026"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD2","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"Pricing & AI cost","weight":"critical","q":"Does Pro's ₹299 price stay, and which model runs the edits and the blueprints?","lede":"Sonnet 5 for everything costs ₹321 to ₹367 a Pro month against ₹246 net of tax and the payment fee.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":210,"cols":[{"title":"Split routing, ₹299","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Sonnet everywhere, price up"},{"title":"Sonnet everywhere, ₹299 kept"}],"rows":[{"label":"Net cost per Pro user a month","cells":["About ₹184","₹321 to ₹367","₹321 to ₹367"]},{"label":"Price to the customer","cells":["₹299, unchanged","₹499 or more, or caps cut","₹299, unchanged"]},{"label":"Margin before fixed costs","cells":["About ₹60","Positive, at the higher price","About minus ₹120"]}],"note":"₹246.33 is ₹299 net of 18% GST and Razorpay's fee.","caption":"Three ways to close the gap between ₹299 and the model bill."},"stakes":"Every Pro user either earns the studio about ₹60 or costs it about ₹120, on one routing choice.","state":["At the caps, Sonnet 5 for everything costs ₹321.47 on the eleven-file blueprint, ₹367 on the fourteen-file one.","₹299 nets ₹246.33 after 18% GST and Razorpay's 2.36% fee.","Haiku 4.5 for edits and Sonnet 5 batch for blueprints costs about ₹184."],"tension":["Every twelve-month scenario on Sonnet-for-everything loses money at ₹299.","Raising the price or cutting the caps both change what was already promised to the first users."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Split routing: Haiku for edits, Sonnet batch for blueprints","gains":["Keeps ₹299.","About ₹60 margin a Pro user."],"costs":["Two models to maintain and monitor."],"system":"A routing rule per call type.","screens":"No change.","money":"About ₹60 margin per Pro user a month."},{"k":"b","label":"Sonnet 5 for everything, price to ₹499 or more","gains":["One model, simpler support."],"costs":["₹200 higher than the plan promised."],"system":"No change.","screens":"S29 price line changes.","money":"Margin turns positive at the higher price."},{"k":"c","label":"Sonnet 5 for everything at ₹299, caps cut to 50 edits and 3 blueprints","gains":["One model, simpler support."],"costs":["A visible downgrade to the free-to-Pro promise."],"system":"No change.","screens":"S29 caps line changes.","money":"Margin recovers as usage falls."},{"k":"d","label":"Keep ₹299, the caps and Sonnet, and absorb the loss","gains":["Nothing changes for a user."],"costs":["About ₹120 lost per active Pro user a month."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"About minus ₹120 per active Pro user a month."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Split routing is the only option that keeps every promise already made.","The margin is thin but positive, and caching is still unmeasured."],"flip":"A week of real caching data showing Sonnet's cost after cache hits would reopen this.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 2","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 22, the financial model"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD5","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"What the product is","weight":"critical","q":"Is frontmatter a markdown editor for the agent era, or the best markdown app in the world?","lede":"The plan took this sentence implicitly; the decision set reserved it for the founders to state.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"The plan's sentence","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Best markdown app"}],"rows":[{"label":"Customer group","cells":["People whose documents are increasingly agent-written","Every note-taker, a much larger group"]},{"label":"Where Ideas sits","cells":["Its own tab, ahead of the editor","Moves behind the editor, every phase"]},{"label":"Competing set named","cells":["CodeGuide, HackMD, docs-as-code tools","Obsidian, Notion, every note app"]}],"caption":"The sentence decides who the product is competing against."},"stakes":"Every phase's build order, and the two competitors already named in the plan, follow from which sentence wins.","state":["Revision 4 took K1 implicitly; the audit flagged it as reserved to the founders.","The plan's current sentence: a markdown editor for people whose documents are increasingly written with, and for, AI agents."],"tension":["The wider sentence reaches more people today, at the cost of the agent-era focus already built toward.","Changing K1 late moves Ideas in every phase, not just the home screen."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep the plan's sentence","gains":["Matches everything already built and screened."],"costs":["A smaller starting customer group."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Adopt 'the best markdown note-taking app in the world'","gains":["A much larger addressable group from day one."],"costs":["Ideas moves behind the editor in every phase."],"system":"No change.","screens":"Every screen's ordering of Ideas changes.","money":"No change named."},{"k":"c","label":"Write a different sentence","gains":["Fits a candidate not yet on the table."],"costs":["Every downstream section needs a fresh pass."],"system":"No change.","screens":"Depends on the sentence.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The plan, the screens and the research already argue for the agent-era sentence.","Nothing in the corpus argues the wider claim; adopting it would be asserted, not evidenced."],"flip":"Twenty kit recipients naming general note-taking, not agent workflows, as their reason to stay would overturn this.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 5","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 1"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD6","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"What the product is","weight":"critical","q":"Do we hold every cloud document from phase A, or carry the pilot on the desktop and hold only shared pages?","lede":"Card K2 said hold as little as possible for as little time as possible; sign-in-first with cloud documents on Free makes that hard to keep.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":200,"cols":[{"title":"Hold from phase A","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Desktop-first pilot"}],"rows":[{"label":"Where phase F, the desktop app, sits","cells":["After Drive sync, later in the sequence","Moves before phase A"]},{"label":"What the free caps mean before sync ships","cells":["Meaningful from day one","Nothing, until sync exists"]},{"label":"Data held","cells":["Every cloud document, from the first sign-in","Only what a person chooses to share"]}],"caption":"Sign-in first collides with holding as little as possible."},"stakes":"This decides whether phase F, the desktop app, comes before or after phase A, the door.","state":["The plan holds every document on R2 and Supabase from day one.","Card K2 recommended holding as little as possible, for as little time as possible.","Sign-in first and cloud documents on Free make holding from phase A close to unavoidable."],"tension":["A desktop-first pilot delays the free caps having any meaning until sync ships.","Holding from phase A needs the deletion, export and retention rules written before a stranger signs in."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Hold every cloud document from phase A, under stated retention rules","gains":["The plan's build order stays as sequenced."],"costs":["More data held, sooner, than K2's own recommendation."],"system":"Deletion, export and retention rules ship with phase A.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Desktop carries the pilot; the web holds only shared pages until sync exists","gains":["Matches K2's instinct to hold little, for a while."],"costs":["Phase F moves before phase A."],"system":"Sync becomes a phase-A dependency instead of phase F's.","screens":"S25, desktop, moves earlier in the flow.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Sign-in first was already decided, and it makes minimal holding impractical.","The retention rules the audit asked for now exist in the data model section."],"flip":"A founder deciding sign-in-first was itself the wrong call reopens this from the other end.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 6","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 18, the data model"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD3","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"Pricing & AI cost","weight":"high","q":"Does the free AI chain add a provider that trains on documents, or hold the line at four?","lede":"The sign-in page promises 'We never train on your documents'; one candidate provider's terms were never opened to check that.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":5,"nodes":[{"label":"Groq","note":"free tier, no training stated","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Cloudflare Workers AI","note":"10,000 neurons a day","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Cerebras","note":"30-day trial","tone":"warn"},{"label":"SambaNova","note":"production models","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Local model","note":"desktop app only","tone":"sunk"}],"note":"No OpenRouter endpoint until its terms are opened and quoted.","caption":"The free chain in fallback order, as the plan runs it today."},"stakes":"The sign-in page's promise is only as true as the weakest provider in the fallback chain.","state":["Groq, Cloudflare Workers AI and SambaNova's production models state no training in pages opened by research.","Cerebras is a 30-day trial behind a payment method.","OpenRouter's Nvidia-served endpoint carried an unverified training flag; its terms were never opened."],"tension":["About 260 active free users is where Cloudflare's free neurons run out and start costing money.","Adding a training-permitted provider means rewriting the sign-in promise, not just the chain."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Hold the chain at Groq, Cloudflare, Cerebras and SambaNova","gains":["The sign-in promise stays true as written."],"costs":["Paid Cloudflare neurons from about 260 active free users."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"Cloudflare overage from about 260 free users."},{"k":"b","label":"Add OpenRouter once its terms are opened and quoted with no training","gains":["A wider free pool."],"costs":["Blocks on someone actually opening those terms."],"system":"One more provider adapter.","screens":"No change.","money":"Depends on the provider's own free tier."},{"k":"c","label":"Add a provider that trains, and change the sign-in promise","gains":["A wider free pool immediately."],"costs":["The line becomes conditional: some providers may train."],"system":"One more provider adapter.","screens":"S01 fine print changes.","money":"Depends on the provider's own free tier."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["This is the only option that needs nobody to check anything first.","The promise on the sign-in page stays literally true."],"flip":"OpenRouter's terms being opened and read as no-training adds it back with no promise to rewrite.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 3","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 14, AI for the pilot"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD8","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"Engine","weight":"high","q":"Does live editing stay in phase D on the CRDT exception, or move to Later?","lede":"Yjs is a CRDT; the plan says never a CRDT and uses Yjs elsewhere, so the exception has to be written down, not assumed.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"File on disk","meta":"only source of truth","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Two open it","via":"live session starts","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Yjs holds it","meta":"in memory only","via":"while both stay open","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Save is a splice","meta":"session state gone","via":"either side saves","tone":"good"}],"note":"Nothing from the session persists past the save.","caption":"The exception: session state never reaches disk."},"stakes":"This is the one place the plan's own sync rule and its live-editing feature can look like they contradict each other.","state":["Yjs is a CRDT by construction.","The exception: session state lives only while two people have the file open; every save is a splice.","Revision 3 carried this exception paragraph; revision 4 dropped it; revision 5 restores it."],"tension":["A CRDT ban with a live CRDT feature reads as a contradiction unless the exception is on the record.","Cutting live editing removes the only feature the three-collaborator cap actually measures live."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep live editing in phase D, on the written exception","gains":["The three-collaborator cap keeps its live meaning."],"costs":["The exception has to hold under scrutiny."],"system":"No change; Yjs stays session-only, never persisted.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Cut live editing to Later","gains":["No exception to defend."],"costs":["The three-collaborator cap becomes a sharing cap, not a live one."],"system":"Phase D loses its Yjs dependency, shrinks by about a week.","screens":"S19, live collaboration, moves to Later.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The exception is real and narrow: nothing from the session ever reaches disk.","Cutting a shipped-feeling feature to defend a rule against a hypothetical reading costs more than keeping it."],"flip":"A working session surviving a crash with state intact would mean Yjs is persisting something, and the exception would no longer hold.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 8","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 21, sync"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD9","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"Free & Pro","weight":"high","q":"Are the free caps 50 documents, 5 pages and 3 collaborators, or the founders' original 5, 2 and 1?","lede":"A blueprint alone is fifteen files; the market floor across the forty pricing pages examined is 50 documents.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":160,"cols":[{"title":"50 / 5 / 3","tone":"accent"},{"title":"5 / 2 / 1"}],"rows":[{"label":"Cloud documents","cells":["50","5"]},{"label":"Published pages","cells":["5","2"]},{"label":"Live collaborators","cells":["3","1"]},{"label":"One blueprint alone","cells":["Fits inside the cap","Blows past the cap on its own"]}],"caption":"The founders' original numbers do not fit one blueprint."},"stakes":"A cap a single blueprint cannot fit inside blocks the idea funnel on day one, for every free user.","state":["The market floor across forty pricing pages examined is 50 free documents; nobody caps public pages by count.","A blueprint is fifteen files by itself.","A downgraded account keeps every document readable and exportable, and cannot create new ones until under the cap."],"tension":["5 documents blocks the import funnel and the idea funnel on day one.","50 is generous against the market floor, which argues the studio should say why, not just what."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"50 documents, 5 published pages, 3 live collaborators","gains":["A blueprint fits inside the free cap.","Sits at the market floor, not below it."],"costs":["Higher than the founders' first candidates."],"system":"No change.","screens":"S33, over cap, uses these numbers.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"5 documents, 2 published pages, 1 live collaborator","gains":["Matches the founders' original candidates."],"costs":["Blocks the import and idea funnels on day one."],"system":"No change.","screens":"S33 and the idea screens change their blocking point.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["No blueprint can be tried at all under the founders' original numbers.","Fifty sits exactly at the floor forty pricing pages already set, not above it."],"flip":"Evidence that free users at 50 documents never convert would argue for a tighter cap.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 9","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 13, free and Pro"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD14","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"Phase 0","weight":"high","q":"Does phase 0 return with twenty hand-made kits before phase C, or does Ideas ship on conviction?","lede":"An earlier revision gated everything on twenty hand-made kits; a later one dropped the gate without a record.","visual":{"kind":"funnel","steps":[{"label":"Kits made by hand","n":20,"unit":"people","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Run the kickoff prompt","n":5,"unit":"of 20","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Edit the kit again","n":2,"unit":"of 10","tone":"stop"}],"note":"The stop and continue lines in question 15 are read off this same funnel.","caption":"What happens to twenty hand-made kits, if the gate returns."},"stakes":"Building on conviction instead of this funnel is exactly what the 13 September reset and the earlier revision both existed to stop.","state":["An earlier plan gated Ideas on twenty hand-made kits for people outside the studio.","A later revision dropped the gate with no note explaining why.","Five of twenty running the kickoff prompt, two of ten editing the kit again, are the pass line."],"tension":["Twenty kits by hand is real founder time before any code for phase C is written.","Shipping on conviction risks repeating whatever made the studio reverse an earlier cut in the first place."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Phase 0 returns: twenty hand-made kits before phase C starts","gains":["The gate that reversed an earlier cut is back in force."],"costs":["Founder time on kits instead of code."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change; phase C waits on this gate.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Ideas ships on conviction; the kill line moves to the pilot","gains":["Phase C starts sooner."],"costs":["No outside-the-studio signal before building it."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["This exact gate is why the generator and kickoff prompt exist in the plan at all.","Twenty kits by hand is a small cost against building Ideas on nothing but conviction."],"flip":"A founder judging the earlier reversal to have been wrong reopens this from the root.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 14","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 26, the build in appetites"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD11","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"Everywhere","weight":"medium","q":"Does the desktop app ship after Drive sync, or first, and who signs the Windows build?","lede":"Azure Artifact Signing excludes Indian entities; an Apple developer programme seat is 99 US dollars a year.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":140,"cols":[{"title":"After Drive sync","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Desktop first"}],"rows":[{"label":"macOS","cells":["Signed, on the Apple programme","Signed, on the Apple programme"]},{"label":"Linux","cells":["Unsigned, by choice","Unsigned, by choice"]},{"label":"Windows","cells":["Shown as coming, certificate unpriced","Answered before the app ships"]},{"label":"Phase order","cells":["F after E, as sequenced","F moves before E"]}],"caption":"The Windows question is the same either way; only its timing changes."},"stakes":"Shipping Windows unsigned trades a security warning on every install for skipping a certificate cost nobody has priced.","state":["Azure Artifact Signing, Microsoft's own signing route, excludes Indian entities.","An Apple Developer Programme seat is 99 US dollars a year, and covers macOS signing.","A commercial Windows certificate has not been priced in this plan."],"tension":["Shipping first without a Windows answer forces the real decision mid-build instead of before it.","Waiting for Drive sync delays every desktop-only user by however long sync takes."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Ship after Drive sync, macOS signed, Windows shown as coming","gains":["Follows the sequence already argued in the plan."],"costs":["A Windows user waits with no signed build."],"system":"No change.","screens":"S25 keeps its current place.","money":"A Windows certificate, priced before it is needed."},{"k":"b","label":"Ship the desktop app first, answer Windows before, not after","gains":["Desktop-only users are not waiting on sync."],"costs":["A certificate decision is forced now, not later."],"system":"Phase F moves ahead of phase E.","screens":"S25 moves earlier in the flow.","money":"A Windows certificate, priced now."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Nothing in the pace evidence argues for reordering the phases yet.","A Windows certificate is a cost to shop for, not to decide under pressure."],"flip":"A pilot cohort skewed heavily toward desktop-only Windows users would argue for moving the phase and the certificate up.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 11","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 12, offline, desktop, phone"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD17","cat":"Gates the plan","sub":"Growth","weight":"medium","q":"Should a published page be indexed by search engines, kept out always, or switched on by its author?","lede":"The plan names no growth channel other than search, and the shipped code keeps every published page out of it.","visual":{"kind":"flow","perRow":5,"nodes":[{"label":"A page is published","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"robots.ts disallows /p/","note":"today's default","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Indexed by default"},{"label":"Never indexed"},{"label":"Author switches it on"}],"note":"The last three are the three options, not a sequence.","caption":"Today's default, and the three ways to change it."},"stakes":"This decides whether the product has a second growth channel beyond word of mouth, or has to name one.","state":["robots.ts disallows /p/, so every published page is out of search today.","The plan names no growth channel other than search.","No default was carried into this revision; the audit raised it from the growth angle alone."],"tension":["Indexing by default trades a stranger's privacy expectation for a channel the plan currently lacks.","Staying unindexed means the plan still needs another answer to how anyone finds frontmatter."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Index published pages by default, with an unlisted switch","gains":["A working growth channel from day one."],"costs":["A published page is public-by-default, not private-by-default."],"system":"robots.ts allows /p/; an unlisted flag per page.","screens":"S17, share, gains a visibility toggle.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Never index; the plan names another channel","gains":["A published page stays private unless shared directly."],"costs":["The plan still needs a real answer for growth."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"c","label":"Unlisted by default, indexed only when the author switches it on","gains":["Privacy by default, a channel for whoever wants it."],"costs":["Most authors never find the switch."],"system":"robots.ts allows only switched-on paths.","screens":"S17 gains a visibility toggle, off by default.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"c","recCase":["No other card in this set has to name a growth channel from scratch; this one does.","Unlisted by default costs no privacy and still lets an author opt into search."],"flip":"A pilot with zero organic sign-ups by week four would argue for indexing by default instead.","sources":["docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 29, questions for the founders","src/app/robots.ts, read 17 September 2026"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD4","cat":"Can wait for the build","sub":"Legal","weight":"high","q":"Who is the grievance officer of record while the legal pages are still placeholders?","lede":"All four public legal pages answered 307 to the sign-in wall until this branch shipped placeholders that say the text is pending.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"Sagnik","tone":"accent"},{"title":"Amit"},{"title":"Counsel"}],"rows":[{"label":"Named on the public pages","cells":["Yes, today","If chosen","If engaged"]},{"label":"Legal-row dates move with","cells":["Sagnik's calendar","Amit's calendar","Counsel's engagement"]}],"caption":"Someone has to be named before a stranger reaches these pages."},"stakes":"Nothing publishes to a stranger until this apparatus exists, and the apparatus starts with a name.","state":["curl confirmed on 17 September 2026: /privacy, /terms, /pricing and /refunds each answered 307 to /login.","Placeholder public pages now ship on this branch and say the text is pending.","The legal section carries an owner and a date on every row."],"tension":["Naming an officer now is a small commitment; naming the wrong one moves every date in the legal section.","Counsel as the owner adds a real engagement cost the plan has not priced."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Sagnik is the officer of record","gains":["No new engagement needed."],"costs":["Adds a duty to one founder's existing load."],"system":"No change.","screens":"The public pages name Sagnik.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Amit is the officer of record","gains":["Splits founder duties differently."],"costs":["The legal-row dates move to Amit's calendar."],"system":"No change.","screens":"The public pages name Amit.","money":"No change."},{"k":"c","label":"Counsel is engaged and named","gains":["A professional handles grievance response."],"costs":["A new, unpriced engagement."],"system":"No change.","screens":"The public pages name counsel.","money":"Counsel's fee, not yet priced."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Sagnik is already named in the branch that shipped the placeholders.","Changing it later is a one-line edit, not a rebuild."],"flip":"Counsel accepting the role at a priced, acceptable fee would move this to option c.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 4","verify/2026-09-17/RESPONSE.jsonl, F008"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD12","cat":"Can wait for the build","sub":"Legal","weight":"high","q":"Is the stated age floor eighteen, or thirteen with a consent path built before the law requires it?","lede":"The DPDP Rules' consent section comes into force 14 May 2027, eighteen months after the Act's commencement notice.","visual":{"kind":"timeline","items":[{"when":"13 Nov 2025","label":"DPDP Rules 2025 gazetted","tone":"sunk"},{"when":"14 Nov 2025","label":"Commencement notice published","tone":"sunk"},{"when":"17 Sep 2026","label":"Plan states no age; default set to 18","tone":"accent"},{"when":"14 May 2027","label":"Section 9, parental consent, in force","tone":"warn"}],"note":"Eighteen months from the commencement notice's own publication date.","caption":"A real date for the consent duty; the plan's answer need not wait for it."},"stakes":"Choosing thirteen now means building a verifiable-consent path on a schedule the law sets, not one the studio picks.","state":["DPDP section 9 requires verifiable parental consent for anyone under eighteen.","Gazette CG-DL-E-14112025-267647, G.S.R. 843(E): section 9 comes into force eighteen months after 14 November 2025, so 14 May 2027.","The plan states no age floor today."],"tension":["The pilot itself runs and ends before the section is even in force.","Thirteen widens the reachable audience today, at the cost of a consent path that has to exist by the same date."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Eighteen, stated in the terms and the sign-in fine print","gains":["No consent path to build before the pilot."],"costs":["Narrows the reachable audience."],"system":"No change.","screens":"S01 fine print states the floor.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Thirteen, with a consent path built before 14 May 2027","gains":["A wider reachable audience from day one."],"costs":["A verifiable-consent flow, confirmed by counsel, has to ship before that date."],"system":"A parental-consent flow, new build.","screens":"Sign-in gains an age check and a consent step.","money":"No change named."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The pilot ends before section 9 is even in force, so nothing forces this yet.","Eighteen needs zero new engineering before the first stranger signs in."],"flip":"A pilot cohort skewing markedly younger than expected would argue for building the consent path early instead of waiting.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 12","Gazette CG-DL-E-14112025-267647 and CG-DL-E-14112025-267650, read 17 September 2026"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD7","cat":"Can wait for the build","sub":"What the product is","weight":"medium","q":"Does 'frontmatter' stay, given a store listing with 82,819 installs already holds the name?","lede":"The Indian trademark register needs an OTP login by a founder before this can be checked properly.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":170,"cols":[{"title":"frontmatter","tone":"accent"},{"title":"A new name"}],"rows":[{"label":"Store collision","cells":["Front Matter CMS, 82,819 installs","None found yet"]},{"label":"Domain and portfolio path","cells":["Unchanged","frontmatter.in and every @handle change"]},{"label":"Screens affected","cells":["None","Every screen with the wordmark, in a day"]}],"caption":"82,819 installs already sit on a name close enough to collide."},"stakes":"A name change late costs a day of screens; a collision found late after Razorpay goes live costs more.","state":["Front Matter CMS holds the store name with 82,819 installs.","The Indian trademark register needs an OTP login by a founder; it was not checked this session.","The plan carries the collision as a named risk."],"tension":["Waiting for the register search delays certainty; running it now costs one founder's time.","A name change is cheap in screens and expensive in already-shared links and a portfolio path."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Keep 'frontmatter'; a founder runs the register search before Razorpay goes live","gains":["Nothing changes today."],"costs":["Carries the collision as a live risk until checked."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Choose a new name now","gains":["Clears the collision before it can bite."],"costs":["The domain, the published-page URLs and the portfolio path all change."],"system":"No change.","screens":"Every screen with the wordmark changes, in about a day.","money":"A new domain purchase."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The register search costs one OTP login, not a rebuild.","No collision has actually been confirmed yet, only the store listing."],"flip":"A confirmed trademark on the register in the same class would force a new name regardless of preference.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 7","verify/2026-09-17/RESPONSE.jsonl, F008"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD10","cat":"Can wait for the build","sub":"AI","weight":"medium","q":"Does Settings gain a bring-your-own-key field in phase B, or does every call stay operator-paid?","lede":"An earlier research round rated a key field as evidence-backed; a later revision dropped it without a record.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"Settings, AI","tone":"sunk"},{"label":"Key present?","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Calls run on your key"},{"label":"Calls run on the operator chain","tone":"accent"}],"note":"The operator chain is always the fallback.","caption":"Where a call goes, with or without a personal key."},"stakes":"A key field shifts some abuse risk off the free pools and onto whoever brings their own key, for free.","state":["An earlier research round rated a key field as evidence-backed.","A later revision dropped the field with no record of why.","Today, the abuse risk of the free chain is carried by the sign-in wall alone."],"tension":["A key field is a small phase-B addition against an abuse surface that has never been priced.","Operator-paid only keeps the breaker simple, at the cost of dropping an evidence-backed feature."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Add a bring-your-own-key field in Settings, phase B","what":"For Anthropic and any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.","gains":["A person's own calls run through their key when present."],"costs":["A new field to secure and support."],"system":"A key field, encrypted at rest.","screens":"Settings AI gains one field.","money":"Shifts some cost off the operator's free pools."},{"k":"b","label":"Operator-paid only","gains":["The per-account breaker stays simple."],"costs":["Drops a feature the research already rated evidence-backed."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The research already rated this evidence-backed once; nothing has reversed that.","A key field is contained scope for phase B, not a new phase."],"flip":"A security review finding key storage cannot be done safely at this stage would move this to option b.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 10","verify/2026-09-17/RESPONSE.jsonl, F056"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD13","cat":"Can wait for the build","sub":"Ownership","weight":"medium","q":"Which accounts move to the company before the first rupee, and which stay personal by choice?","lede":"The Cloudflare zone sits on a personal account by choice; the domain, Razorpay, Apple and the provider accounts were otherwise unnamed.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Personal today","meta":"the zone, by choice","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Company, first rupee","via":"zone, domain, Razorpay","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Company, phase F","via":"Apple, providers","tone":"good"}],"note":"The zone's split is deliberate; the rest was simply never named.","caption":"What moves when, under the plan's own ownership table."},"stakes":"An account still on a founder's personal name when Razorpay goes live is a real business risk, not a paperwork one.","state":["AGENTS.md records the Cloudflare zone on a personal account as a deliberate split.","The domain, Razorpay, Apple and the provider accounts were unnamed in the plan until this revision.","An ownership table now exists, with a mover and a date on every row."],"tension":["Moving everything before the first rupee is the safest reading, and the slowest one.","Naming exceptions honestly costs nothing except admitting a founder's name is still on record somewhere."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Move zone, domain and Razorpay now; Apple and providers at phase F","gains":["Matches the ownership table already in the plan."],"costs":["Some accounts wait until phase F to move."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Name which accounts stay personal, and why","gains":["Honest about what will not move."],"costs":["A named risk row for each exception."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["This is the plan's own table, not a new proposal.","Money-handling accounts move first; everything else follows at a named phase."],"flip":"A founder wanting to keep the domain personally, for tax or other reasons, would move this to option b, named.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 13","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 24, ownership and accounts"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD15","cat":"Can wait for the build","sub":"The pilot","weight":"medium","q":"Do the audit's stop and continue lines hold for the twenty-person pilot, or do the founders set their own?","lede":"An earlier revision's pilot section listed measures with no thresholds at all.","visual":{"kind":"compare","labelWidth":210,"cols":[{"title":"Stop","tone":"stop"},{"title":"Continue","tone":"good"}],"rows":[{"label":"Active in week two","cells":["Fewer than 4 of 20","6 of 20 or more"]},{"label":"Kit recipients who run the kickoff","cells":["Fewer than 2 of 10","3 of 10 or more"]},{"label":"Name the problem unprompted","cells":["Fewer than 3 of 20","One person asks how to pay"]}],"caption":"The same twenty-person pilot, read for a reason to stop or continue."},"stakes":"A pilot with no numbers attached to it cannot fail, and a plan that cannot fail is not being tested.","state":["An earlier revision listed pilot measures with no thresholds.","The audit's design sizes both lines to the same twenty-person pilot and ten kit recipients."],"tension":["Any threshold the founders pick is at least as defensible as the audit's; the only failure is picking none.","Setting the bar too low makes a weak pilot look like a pass."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Adopt the audit's stop and continue lines","gains":["A number exists before the pilot starts, not after."],"costs":["Not the founders' own judgement call."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Set different numbers","gains":["Reflects the founders' own risk appetite."],"costs":["Needs deciding before the pilot, not during it."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The lines are sized to the pilot the plan already describes.","Adopting a number now is strictly better than the section that had none."],"flip":"A founder judging four of twenty active as too easy a bar would justify tightening it before the pilot starts.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 15","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 28, what we measure"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD16","cat":"Can wait for the build","sub":"Product history","weight":"medium","q":"Does the Zed rebuttal, the dropped review sidecar, and the deferred extension, community and Max tier all stand as this revision has them?","lede":"Zed Delta now stakes span-level attribution on CRDTs in public, against the plan's own settled sync position.","visual":{"kind":"state","states":[{"label":"Review sidecar","meta":"dropped","tone":"stop"},{"label":"Change queue","meta":"adopted instead","via":"17 Sep 2026","tone":"accent"},{"label":"Zed rebuttal","meta":"owed","via":"before phase D","tone":"warn"}],"note":"The extension, community and the Max tier stay deferred, named, not decided.","caption":"What changed, what is owed, and what stays deferred."},"stakes":"Leaving the Zed rebuttal unwritten leaves the plan's sync position undefended in public against a named competitor.","state":["Review state is dropped in favour of the change queue, and the plan now says so.","The extension form factor, the community and the Max tier are deferred and named, not decided.","The written rebuttal to Zed Delta's public CRDT bet is still owed."],"tension":["Writing the rebuttal before phase D is cheap; not writing it leaves the sync position looking undefended.","Bringing any deferred item back now competes with everything already sequenced."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"As this revision has them: rebuttal before D, sidecar dropped, rest deferred","gains":["Matches the plan as written today."],"costs":["The rebuttal is a real, unscheduled piece of writing."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Bring one deferred item back now","gains":["Whichever item returns gets a real phase."],"costs":["The phase table absorbs whatever comes back."],"system":"Depends on which item.","screens":"Depends on which item.","money":"No change named."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["Nothing in this revision's evidence argues for reviving a deferred item early.","The rebuttal is the one open item with an actual deadline: before phase D."],"flip":"A customer naming Zed Delta by name as a reason not to choose frontmatter would move the rebuttal from owed to urgent.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 16","CLAUDE.md, settled positions, the sync caveat"],"linked":[]},{"id":"FD18","cat":"Can wait for the build","sub":"Account","weight":"medium","q":"Does an email magic link sit beside Google and GitHub as the fallback sign-in, or do the two providers stand alone?","lede":"The stack section names Google and GitHub as providers and leaves the fallback sign-in for the founders to decide.","visual":{"kind":"flow","nodes":[{"label":"Google"},{"label":"GitHub"},{"label":"Email magic link","dashed":true,"note":"the fallback in question","tone":"warn"}],"caption":"Two providers are settled; the third path is the open question."},"stakes":"Without a fallback, anyone without a Google or GitHub account has no way to sign in at all.","state":["The stack section names Google and GitHub as sign-in providers.","An email magic link is named as the founders' fallback candidate, not yet decided."],"tension":["A fallback reaches people with neither account; it also adds one more sign-in path to secure and support.","Two providers alone is simpler, and excludes anyone who uses neither."],"options":[{"k":"a","label":"Add an email magic link beside Google and GitHub","gains":["Reaches people with neither account."],"costs":["One more sign-in path to secure and support."],"system":"A magic-link flow through the auth provider.","screens":"S01 gains a third sign-in option.","money":"No change."},{"k":"b","label":"Google and GitHub only","gains":["Two providers, nothing else to secure."],"costs":["Excludes anyone with neither account."],"system":"No change.","screens":"No change.","money":"No change."}],"rec":"a","recCase":["The plan's own stack section already names this as the founders' candidate.","A locked-out sign-up is the more expensive failure to leave open."],"flip":"Evidence that the pilot's twenty people all already hold a Google or GitHub account would remove the need.","sources":["docs/mvp0/DECISIONS-FOR-FOUNDERS-2026-09-17.md, question 18","docs/mvp0/PRODUCT-PLAN.md, section 15, the stack"],"linked":[]}];
